# Basic Memory schema notes — use BM-specific notation ([category], [[wiki-links]])
# that remark's no-undefined-references rule cannot parse.
schemas/

# Sprint retrospectives — gitignored, local-only, use BM-style [category] prose
# and >NN constructs that trip no-undefined-references / no-blockquote-without-marker.
RETRO-*.md

# Swarm-wave sprint state — gitignored, ephemeral scratch; agent-assignment lines
# use [P1]/[P2]/[P3] priority tags that remark reads as undefined link references.
SWARM-*.md

# Plan / design working drafts — gitignored, local-only; same bracket-prose hazard.
PLAN-*.md

# Skill/tool evaluation records — gitignored, local-only; use BM-style [category]
# and outcome tags like [version]/fixed[version] that trip no-undefined-references.
evaluations/

# Local clone / scratch dirs — untracked vendored checkouts (_tmp_*,
# _research_dashboard, _kimchi_tmp, _astgrep_tmp, _polint_tmp, _tmp_atelier,
# _tmp_narumiruna, _tmp_pi_monorepo, _tmp_powerline, _tmp_zentui) pulled in for
# cross-referencing. Their own markdown + tooling is not part of this repo; a bare
# `remark .` was walking every file in them (thousands of errors + EAGAIN spawns),
# masking this repo's own lint. All such dirs start with an underscore and are
# untracked, so `_*`/` touches nothing tracked (verified via `git ls-files`).
# CI's fresh clone has none of them, so the exclusion is a no-op there.
_*/

# Frozen sweep inputs + the preserved batch-1 report — gitignored working data
# with a known expiry, kept as the offline oracle for `rank.mjs` replays.
#
# The report in here is a HISTORICAL artefact and must stay byte-identical: its
# two `no-literal-urls` warnings (`npm-@jazzer.js-core` parsing as a GFM email
# autolink) are exactly the defect since fixed at source by code-spanning the
# Note column. Linting a frozen record of a fixed bug would only ever produce
# pressure to edit the record.
.baseline-*/

# Generated staleness report — gitignored, regenerated per run. Excluded so the
# repo-wide `check:md` does not depend on a generated artefact being present.
#
# The original rationale here was WRONG on both halves, measured 2026-08-05:
#   * "`[category]` tokens trip no-undefined-references" — the real report
#     produces ZERO such findings. Every `[category]` token in it sits inside a
#     backtick code span, where `[` is literal; that escaping contract is stated
#     at the point of construction in rank.mjs.
#   * "the workflow validates this file explicitly with `--rc-path`, so it is
#     not left unchecked" — it was left unchecked. remark refuses an explicitly
#     named ignored file with `Cannot process specified file: it's ignored` and
#     exits 1, so from the moment this entry was added the workflow's validation
#     step reported a failure that had nothing to do with markdown quality.
#
# The workflow therefore passes `--no-ignore`, which is what makes this entry
# scope-limiting rather than validation-disabling. Do not remove that flag.
# With it, the report's only real findings were two `no-literal-urls` warnings —
# `npm-@jazzer.js-core` parsing as a GFM email autolink — now fixed at source by
# code-spanning the Note column.
stale-npm-triage.md
